From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 22:12:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gateway: a provider's failWords fail a 200 that is only its
 pitch for a spent plan (#5692)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A relay that has spent its plan and answers with a 200 and a pitch of
its own — finish reason stop, the usage counted, no word of error —
went to the agent as the answer it isn't: an agent asking for JSON had
a JSONDecodeError, one asking for code an advert, request after
request, while every page said 200, for as long as the plan was spent
(leavrcn). failure reads a try that has failed already (carriedStatus),
holdWriter.failed wants a status of its own (400 up), errorReply an
error envelope with no choices beside it, and saidAnything a Text part
saying — nothing of the five covers a completion that is legally one.

failWords are the words a whole reply of a success status is read by,
per provider, off by default: nothing is read of a reply a user hasn't
opted in for, the same words in a real answer failing it being that
user's own to weigh. The words are read as they are written, never as
a guess of what a pitch says (#5089's rule); one magpie can't read is
dropped, not fatal. A reply saying one of them fails as its own words
stand for (streamStatus), asked of the next member, the account rested
as the vendor's own 429 would rest it; nobody left, the agent is told
the failure, never handed the pitch. Set in providers.json by hand; a
save of the editor's, whose form doesn't carry them, keeps what was
stored. The reply as it streams, whose first content is let through
for its TTFT, is not read: a pitch that went out stays out, and the
rest keeps the next request away.

